/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://a.pool.opentimestamps.org https://b.pool.opentimestamps.org https://a.pool.eternitywall.com https://finney.calendar.eternitywall.com https://api.ipify.org https://api6.ipify.org https://overpass-api.de https://maps.mail.ru; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), geolocation=(self), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# `media-src` must name blob: explicitly. Recorded video is previewed and sampled for the
# report through a blob: URL, and without this it falls back to default-src 'self', which
# blocks it. Caught only in production -- the dev server ships no CSP at all.
#
# `data:` is present in font-src because jsPDF inlines its standard font metrics as
# data: URIs to measure text; blocking them silently degrades line wrapping in the PDF.
# It cannot be used to exfiltrate anything — a data: URI carries no network request.
#
# `connect-src` also names api.ipify.org / api6.ipify.org (the footer's IPv4/IPv6 lookup —
# see useMyIp.ts) and overpass-api.de plus its maps.mail.ru mirror (the nearby mosque/police
# search — see NearbyResourcesSection.tsx / nearbyPlaces.ts). Same blind spot as media-src
# above: the dev server ships no CSP, so a missing host here only ever shows up in production,
# as a fetch that silently fails with nothing in the console pointing at why. The mirror is
# there because the primary is a single shared public server that rate-limits by IP and drops
# CORS headers on throttled responses — nearbyPlaces.ts falls back to it. See that file's own
# comment for why this particular mirror, and not one of three others that looked fine but
# turned out broken in ways that don't show up as an error (silent 500s, a User-Agent
# allowlist that blocks every real browser, or a 200 response with an empty database).
#
# `Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self)` — not `()` — for the same reason: `()` blocks the
# Geolocation API outright, so `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition` in useGeolocation.ts
# would reject as if permission were denied before the browser ever showed its own prompt.
# `(self)` still requires the ordinary per-visit browser permission prompt; it only lifts the
# origin-level block.

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The service worker script must be revalidated on every load, or the CDN's default
# caching would delay how quickly an updated worker (and its cache-cleanup logic) reaches
# already-installed clients.
